{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I want that relaxed blues feel today.",
    "Step Back and Let Me Get By connect with the blues guitar and soulful roots sound I enjoyed in Memphis and People, Hell & Angels; Croz and Plain Spoken also fit my interest in reflective songwriting."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Heaven & Earth and The Endless River miss my current mood: progressive rock and atmospheric instrumentals do not offer the blues feel and songwriting I want right now.",
    "I cannot confidently connect the unspecified Led Zeppelin release to what I want to hear, so I would pass during a brief visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that an interest in established rock musicians means I want their music across very different styles.",
    "Expressive guitar playing alone is not enough to make something my next choice; Rattle That Lock appeals to me less immediately than the relaxed blues of The Breeze."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in Old Sock matters especially today because I am looking for an easygoing blues listen.",
    "Blown Away makes the country direction of Cass County relevant, but that is a secondary interest for this visit; I would choose only one album, even when several feel compatible."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in blues and roots songwriting, but stretched it too broadly into rock choices that do not match today's listening mood."
}"}
